Sketch of `exemplar`.

Mostly complete, but need to work with it to find the edge cases and determine
if it is not too clever. Likely not and likely to make it easier to write the
pipeline automations, increasing the amount of code eligible for syntax
highlighting.

One potential problem is that line continuations, (i.e. '\\n') are eliminated,
so we are stuck with very long lines that are going to to wrap in the
terminal, instead of long commands being nicely-formatted with multiple lines.
One would think that it was more important for the pipeline automation display
to be just so, but knocking down the complexity of the pipeline code for a
couple of run-on lines in the pipeline console display is probably worth it
when we don't really care about the details pipeline display unless there is
an error. We'll still have our debugging and our ability to copy and paste a
command to our own terminal. Most of the time the spew is merely to see that
the pipeline is making progress, not to spot a pull request viewer as a `gh`
command goes by.

This merging of multi-lines would have been a deal breaker a couple years ago.
